<!-- Phase 5 website teaching layer; original chapter remains read-only. Evidence: website/reviews/android-phase5-findings.md. -->

<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">The first import looks correct. A retry duplicates a workout, and a deleted record comes back from your app’s cache. Health synchronization needs a repeatable local transaction: which records changed, which disappeared, and how far has the import safely committed?</p>

<!-- @after Incremental Synchronization :: animation -->
### Commit data before advancing progress

<figure class="stepper" data-illustrated data-no-handoff><span class="stepper-title">One incremental page, with a crash in the middle</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="node" data-el="token" data-art="document" data-art-role="storage"><strong>Saved progress</strong><small data-text="tokenV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="page" data-art="document" data-art-role="storage"><strong>Changes page</strong><small data-text="pageV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="db" data-art="database" data-art-role="storage"><strong>App-owned store</strong><small data-text="dbV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
{
"label": "Fetch",
"caption": "Read the next changes page using saved progress T1.",
"state": {
"page": "active"
},
"text": {
"tokenV": "T1",
"pageV": "upsert A; delete B; next T2",
"dbV": "previous state"
},
"add": [
"token",
"page",
"db"
]
},
{
"label": "Apply",
"caption": "Apply upserts and deletions to local storage.",
"state": {
"db": "active"
},
"text": {
"dbV": "A updated; B removed"
}
},
{
"label": "Crash before commit",
"caption": "If the local transaction fails before committing data and progress, replay from the last committed token while it remains valid; otherwise take the reconciliation path.",
"state": {
"db": "warn",
"token": "done"
},
"text": {
"dbV": "transaction rolled back",
"tokenV": "still T1"
}
},
{
"label": "Replay and commit",
"caption": "An idempotent transaction can apply the page again and commit its matching progress.",
"state": {
"db": "done",
"token": "active"
},
"text": {
"dbV": "A updated; B removed",
"tokenV": "T2 after success"
}
},
{
"label": "Token no longer usable",
"caption": "Use the chapter’s bounded reconciliation path when progress expires or is invalid.",
"state": {
"token": "warn"
},
"text": {
"tokenV": "reconcile; do not invent missing history"
}
}
]</script><figcaption>The transaction pattern is application design. Feature availability, permission scope and historical coverage still bound what can be read.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Testing Strategy :: check -->
### Try the decision

<details><summary>No steps returned. User inactive?</summary>

Not necessarily: missing access, data, availability or synchronization can also explain it.
</details>

<details><summary>Token saved before local writes?</summary>

A crash could skip changes. Save matching progress only with successful local application.
</details>

<details><summary>A worker always reads Health Connect?</summary>

Only with the required background-read feature and separate grant; otherwise ingest in the foreground.
</details>

<!-- @after Staff-Level Review Questions :: guide -->
<p>Use these answer guidelines to evaluate the feature you are reviewing. The record types, permitted behavior and retention choices depend on that feature.</p>

<div class="blend" data-kind="guide" data-guidance-answer-for="section-staff-level-review-questions" data-question-index="1"><span class="blend-label">Added answer guidance · 1</span><p>Map each user-facing feature to the record types it reads or writes, its operations, and the required grants. Request the permissions that support those needs, and keep manifest declarations and Play Console access declarations aligned. Explain why each requested type is needed.</p><p><a href="https://developer.android.com/health-and-fitness/health-connect/data-types" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Health Connect data types</a> · <a href="https://developer.android.com/health-and-fitness/health-connect/get-started#declare-permissions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Declare permissions</a></p></div>

<div class="blend" data-kind="guide" data-guidance-answer-for="section-staff-level-review-questions" data-question-index="2"><span class="blend-label">Added answer guidance · 2</span><p>Check the current grants before access. Keep permitted features usable and explain which features need additional access; distinguish missing permission from no recorded data. Provide a route to manage access. Test partial grants and later revocation instead of assuming the initial permission result remains valid.</p><p><a href="https://developer.android.com/health-and-fitness/health-connect/get-started#step-4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Request and check permissions</a> · <a href="https://developer.android.com/health-and-fitness/health-connect/ui/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Permissions and data access</a></p></div>

<div class="blend" data-kind="guide" data-guidance-answer-for="section-staff-level-review-questions" data-question-index="3"><span class="blend-label">Added answer guidance · 3</span><p>Use Health Connect's aggregate API for supported totals and metrics, with the intended time range. Activity and Sleep aggregation applies user-selected app priorities when deduplicating; that rule does not cover every record type. If the product needs a custom calculation, document its meaning and how it handles overlapping sources.</p><p><a href="https://developer.android.com/health-and-fitness/health-connect/aggregate-data" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read aggregated data and app-priority behavior</a></p></div>

<div class="blend" data-kind="guide" data-guidance-answer-for="section-staff-level-review-questions" data-question-index="4"><span class="blend-label">Added answer guidance · 4</span><p>For exports, use a stable <code>clientRecordId</code> and appropriate versioning. For imports, retain Health Connect IDs to apply upserts and deletions. As an application design, commit local changes and matching progress together, then test replay after failure so retrying a page converges on the same result.</p><p><a href="https://developer.android.com/health-and-fitness/health-connect/sync-data" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Synchronize data, record IDs and changes</a></p></div>

<div class="blend" data-kind="guide" data-guidance-answer-for="section-staff-level-review-questions" data-question-index="5"><span class="blend-label">Added answer guidance · 5</span><p>List each local and server copy, why it exists, its retention period and its deletion path. These are product decisions to explain in the privacy policy. Health Connect provides deletion APIs for its records; separately define how deletion reaches app-owned copies and how synchronization avoids restoring deleted data.</p><p><a href="https://developer.android.com/health-and-fitness/health-connect/get-started#show-privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explain data use in the privacy policy</a> · <a href="https://developer.android.com/health-and-fitness/health-connect/delete-data" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Delete Health Connect records</a></p></div>
